Stanneg Village  

   During the dark rule of Cair Muhr, Stanneg Village became a key
point in the Dominion, though it was quite small and insignificant
otherwise.  The Western Mountains were a key part in the High Lord's
of Glasgian's following and Cair had moved her forces into the very heart
of the mountains already.  
  The people of Stanneg were used as messengers and runners between the
Muhrian army and the Golden Knights of Glasgian.  The homes were turned
~
S
#11056
Stanneg Inn~
   This is the plainly decorated main room of the Stanneg Inn.  A large
arch to the west leads to a common room where food and drink can be
ordered, and a set of rickety wooden stairs leads up to the rooms.  A
threadbare rug lies in the middle of the floor, plainly well loved by a
cat or two, judging by the amount of hair on it.  Double doors lead
south.
~
